# Audit imported vehicle FBX vertical grounding

Audit the reported vertical offset in imported vehicle FBX files, record its
deterministic cause, and remove or preserve it only from source evidence.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Audit the reported vertical offset in imported vehicle FBX files, record
  its deterministic cause, and remove or preserve it only from source
  evidence.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

Vehicle export already derived vertical grounding from source-authored geometry.
Ordinary vehicles require four road-wheel surfaces bound to `w0` through `w3`;
their lowest finite Y coordinate yields the exact offset applied to all parts,
the unique root bind, and root animation samples. `mono-v` instead grounds its
visible body while preserving four nonvisual authored wheel proxies as deferred
source evidence. No manual editor offset or hardcoded vehicle height
participates in either path.

The vehicle catalog now publishes that cause for each generated FBX as a
`grounding` object containing `source`, `offset_y`, and `root_bone`. Ordinary
vehicles report `road-wheel-surfaces`; `mono-v` reports
`visible-body-with-authored-wheel-proxies`. The technical vehicle contract names
the same two strategies and explains why the source-axis Y translation is
preserved rather than removed.

Fresh stable-Rust validation passed the new catalog-evidence regression, all
vehicle grounding regressions, and the broader vehicle-catalog test filter.
Existing tests prove all parts and the root move together. Root animation
samples receive the same offset, and monorail proxy rest surfaces remain
unchanged.
